cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this service, cite Pixal3D and the service it wraps.
title: Pixal3D image-to-textured-mesh service, native win-64 (pixi)
abstract: >-
  The Stage 7 image -> mesh HTTP service (AGENTS.md, Stage 7 exception) run
  natively on Windows 11 under pixi, with no Docker and no WSL. Nothing is
  vendored: fetch.py clones each source below at its pinned commit into src/
  (gitignored) and applies the patches listed here.


  patches/service-win.patch (interactor-pixal3d-image-to-textured-mesh
  @61df29e): worker_entry.py loads MoGe-3 (moge.model.v3, default
  Ruicheng/moge-3-vitl) instead of MoGe-2, and takes the MoGe and DINOv3
  weights from PIXAL3D_MOGE / PIXAL3D_DINO; server.py writes the geometry
  into the USD layer as UsdGeom.Mesh prims under /Asset/Geometry (points,
  faceVertexCounts/Indices, vertex normals, primvars:st, extent; stage upAxis
  Y, metersPerUnit 1) beside the GLB asset path it already wrote, reports
  per-call seconds and torch peak VRAM, and takes HOST from the environment;
  worker_entry.generate renders its preview views through render_frames with
  an EnvMap (app.py's forest.exr) and keeps the 'shaded' image, because
  render_multiview passes PbrMeshRenderer.render no envmap (TypeError) and
  returns no 'color' key.


  patches/pixal3d-local-aux.patch (Pixal3D @cdbb2bb): NAF is loaded from the
  local patched clone (NAF_REPO, NAF_WEIGHTS) instead of torch.hub's
  valeoai/NAF; PIXAL3D_REMBG_MODEL overrides pipeline.json's gated
  briaai/RMBG-2.0 with ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet_HR-matting (run at Pixal3D's
  1024^2, as gates/7-pixal3d/aux-models/birefnet.md records).


  patches/naf-na2d-block.patch (NAF @37f2dfc): NATTEN has no win-64 build, so
  CrossAttention runs na2d_block, the exact pure-torch neighbourhood attention
  proven in gates/7-pixal3d/aux-models/naf_ref.py (<= 4.6e-7 vs NATTEN), on
  the low-res K/V directly; hubconf.naf takes a local checkpoint_path.


  patches/moge-flexgemm2.patch (MoGe @74fbce0) and
  patches/flexgemm2-own-cache.patch (FlexGEMM @b2fadb2): MoGe-3's refiner
  needs FlexGEMM 2.0 (flex_gemm.nn), whose API Pixal3D's 0.0.1 calls no longer
  exist in; FlexGEMM 2.0 runs pure Triton without its CUDA extension and
  imports itself relatively, so fetch.py exposes it as the package flex_gemm2,
  MoGe imports that name, and its autotune cache moves to ~/.flex_gemm2.


  Binary wheels (not built here): cumesh 1.0, flex_gemm 0.0.1, o_voxel 0.0.1,
  nvdiffrast 0.4.0, nvdiffrec_render 0.0.0, cp311 win_amd64 for Torch 2.8.0 +
  cu128, from visualbruno/ComfyUI-Trellis2 @14597418 wheels/Windows/Torch280
  (sha256 in README.md); utils3d 0.0.2 from LDYang694/Storages release
  20260430 (Pixal3D's own pin); torch/torchvision from download.pytorch.org
  cu128; triton-windows from PyPI.
